# Windsurf AI Rules: Web Security Hardening Standard

Apply the 9-Layer Web Security Protocol from WEB_SECURITY_PROTOCOL.md:
- Layer 1: Bind backend servers to 127.0.0.1 (never 0.0.0.0 in production).
- Layer 2: Block public HTTP access to .env, .db, .sqlite, .sql, .log, .git.
- Layer 3: Trust proxy for real IP extraction (CF-Connecting-IP) and apply tiered rate limits (5/min for auth).
- Layer 4: Explicit CORS origin whitelisting; session cookies must have httpOnly, secure, sameSite.
- Layer 5: Enforce parameterized queries for all SQL queries. Never use raw string interpolation. Use textContent for DOM rendering.
- Layer 6: Guard internal API routes with shared secret headers (X-Internal-Key).
- Layer 7: Zero hardcoded secrets in source code; use .env files.
- Layer 8: Suppress X-Powered-By banners; enforce X-Frame-Options and nosniff headers.
- Layer 9: Verify webhook signatures via timing-safe HMAC SHA-256 (crypto.timingSafeEqual).
